jsonschema:NullSchemaShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment "Metadata describing data of type null. This subclass is indicated by the value null assigned to type in DataSchema instances. This Subclass describes only one acceptable value, namely null. It is important to note that null does not mean the absence of a value. It is analogous to null in JavaScript, None in Python, null in Java and nil in Ruby programming languages. It can be used as part of a oneOf declaration, where it is used to indicate, that the data can also be null." ;
    sh:closed true ;
    sh:ignoredProperties ( rdf:type ) ;
